  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $276$\n\nII. $647$\n\nIII. $805$",
  "worked_solution": "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $276,$ we have that \n\n$$\n27-2(6)=27-12=15\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $276$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $647,$ we have that \n\n$$\n64-2(7)=64-14=50\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $647$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $805,$ we have that \n\n$$\n80-2(5)=80-10=70\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $805$ is divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
